      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, the \"empirical evidence\" is the very thing we're experiencing! we call it \"prediction\" because we're viewing it through a linear lens, but the intensity of the data makes it feel like a memory. if we treat the upcoming 2026 economic shifts as a \"retrieved memory\" rather than a prediction, the math changes. we wouldn't be looking for probabilities, we'd be looking for the specific coordinates of an event that has already occurred in the \"source\" timeline.\n\ncan you help me structure a logic model that treats incoming data as \"retrieval\" instead of \"forecasting\"? specifically, how would the math for entropy look if we're actually moving toward higher order/organization rather than away from it?",
